<programme start="20261020010600 +0000" stop="20261020013400 +0000" channel="Curiosity 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">The Lightbulb Moment</title><sub-title lang="en">Like Button: The Unintended Consenquences of the Facebook Like Button</sub-title><desc lang="en">When first presented with the like button Facebook CEO Mark Zuckerberg worried that a quick thumbs up or down would discourage more meaningful online interaction but eventually his team changed his mind and transformed the world.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p19437807_b_v11_af.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261020013400 +0000" stop="20261020020400 +0000" channel="Curiosity 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">The Lightbulb Moment</title><sub-title lang="en">Cubicle: How the Cubicle Became Universally Hated</sub-title><desc lang="en">The Cubicle was originally designed to set workers free; a futuristic designer named Robert Propst dreamed up the cubicle as a groovy 1960s workplace utopia that would unleash the modern knowledge worker&apos;s vast untapped potential.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p19437807_b_v11_af.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261020020400 +0000" stop="20261020023200 +0000" channel="Curiosity 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">The Lightbulb Moment</title><sub-title lang="en">Barcode: How the Barcode Shaped Our Modern Economy</sub-title><desc lang="en">Barcodes have radically changed global commerce, helping fuel the rise of everything from massive companies like Walmart to world powers like China, and it all started with a man daydreaming on a beach in 1949.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p19437807_b_v11_af.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261020023200 +0000" stop="20261020030200 +0000" channel="Curiosity 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">The Lightbulb Moment</title><sub-title lang="en">Florida: How Real Estate Rogues Invented Florida as We Know It</sub-title><desc lang="en">Florida wasn&apos;t always the Sunshine State; in the 1920s, an army of real estate boosters set out to redefine Florida from an economic backwater to a ritzy vacation destination, sparking a land boom the likes of which America had never seen before.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p19437807_b_v11_af.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261020030200 +0000" stop="20261020033100 +0000" channel="Curiosity 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">The Lightbulb Moment</title><sub-title lang="en">Mauve: The Fake Color That Made Our Modern World</sub-title><desc lang="en">In 1856, a chemistry student accidentally created a strange substance with a rich purple hue; Mauve takes over the fashion industry, make food look more appetizing, and enable stunning advances in medicine.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p19437807_b_v11_af.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261020033100 +0000" stop="20261020040000 +0000" channel="Curiosity 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">The Lightbulb Moment</title><sub-title lang="en">Vanilla: The Bean That Shaped the Future of Food</sub-title><desc lang="en">In 1841 on the small island of Réunion, a 12-year-old slave did something no one had done before; the vanilla bean takes the world by storm, sparking the artificial flavor revolution and forever changing how we eat.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p19437807_b_v11_af.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261020040000 +0000" stop="20261020043000 +0000" channel="Curiosity 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">The Lightbulb Moment</title><sub-title lang="en">The Hollywood Actress That Laid the Groundwork for WiFi</sub-title><desc lang="en">During WWII, Actress Hedy Lamarr, deemed the world&apos;s most beautiful woman, invented a technology that laid the groundwork for the wireless internet of today.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p19437807_b_v11_af.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261020043000 +0000" stop="20261020050000 +0000" channel="Curiosity 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">The Lightbulb Moment</title><sub-title lang="en">Streaming: The Invention That Revolutionized Streaming Video</sub-title><desc lang="en">The early days of online video were plagued by low resolution, stamp-sized video, and unbearable buffering times but that changed when a breakthrough technology revolutionized streaming video and set the foundation for the era of Netflix.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p19437807_b_v11_af.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261020050000 +0000" stop="20261020052900 +0000" channel="Curiosity 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">The Lightbulb Moment</title><sub-title lang="en">Interstate: How the Interstate Connected and Divided America</sub-title><desc lang="en">Dwight Eisenhower&apos;s interstate highway system was the biggest infrastructure project of its time, a bold plan to connect all corners of America and boost the post-war economy, but it also ended up deepening the divide between rich and poor.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p19437807_b_v11_af.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261020052900 +0000" stop="20261020055800 +0000" channel="Curiosity 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">The Lightbulb Moment</title><sub-title lang="en">Edison: How Edison Reinvented Invention</sub-title><desc lang="en">Edison pioneered the world&apos;s first research and development center in Menlo Park and worked with a group of experimenters to methodically zero in on the holy grail of electric light.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p19437807_b_v11_af.jpg"/></programme>
